Project: Fictional ShoeShop — QA Training Exercise
# BUG-001 — Incorrect Product Price in Shopping Cart
Testing Type: Functional Testing
Bug Category: Shopping Cart / Pricing
Severity: High
Priority: High
Bug Status: Open (Training Scenario)
Reproducibility: 2 out of 2 attempts
## Bug Summary
During a simulated e-commerce testing exercise, a product priced at €80 was displayed as €800 in the shopping cart.
## Preconditions
- The fictional ShoeShop website is accessible.
- The user is logged in.
- A product priced at €80 is available.
- The shopping cart is initially empty.
## Steps to Reproduce
- Open the ShoeShop website.
- Log in using valid credentials.
- Select a pair of shoes priced at €80.
- Click Add to Cart.
- Open the shopping cart.
- Check the displayed product price.
## Expected Result
The shopping cart should display the correct product price of €80.
## Actual Result
The shopping cart displays €800 instead of €80.
## Impact
The incorrect price could mislead customers, cause abandoned purchases, and affect customer trust.
## Conclusion
This fictional training scenario demonstrates how to document a pricing defect using clear reproduction steps, expected and actual results, severity, and priority.
